Package: pve-meta-nvidia
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 pve-meta (>= 0.1.3), pve-container, lxc-pve, libnvidia-container-tools
Description: NVIDIA GPUs for unprivileged LXC guests, from pve-meta documents
 A container whose pve-meta document has a gpu subtree gets the host's GPUs
 through LXC's own nvidia hook: the cgroup device rules for the cards it
 selected, the hook line and the NVIDIA_* environment the hook reads. Nothing
 is installed inside the guest.
 .
 Each node publishes its own cards as the gpu prefix file of its node
 directory, so a guest is offered exactly the GPUs of the node it runs on.
 The NVIDIA driver itself is not a dependency: it is installed in several
 ways and is checked for at runtime.
